    {
      "id": 220853,
      "name": "dpt",
      "username": "dpt",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-07-31T11:25:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Dandolo has the correct interpretation. Note that \"you\" is interpreted communally: the spirits as a whole pay that Energy cost in the usual way for choice events (including the aid by Fire).</p><p>It's worded the way it is because the costs are pooled. Eg, if you do damage in 2 lands, it costs 6 Energy; you can pay for that by Forgetting one card with Fire and discarding another. If the Energy costs were separate you wouldn't be able to do that, since you don't get change for overpaying for Events.</p><p>I updated the <a href=\"https://querki.net/u/darker/spirit-island-faq/#!.7w4g8qv\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">relevant FAQ</a>, I hope that clarifies things.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:53:24.969Z",
